WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.040
From Mantis and Drax's adventures in&nbsp;
Hollywood to a terrified Kevin Bacon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.560
and even a special cameo by Kingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.972
the "Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special"&nbsp;
is filled with Christmas cheer…and Easter eggs.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.540
Marvel Studios has gotten more creative with&nbsp;
its opening credits sequences in Phase 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.400
especially with music cues. "Eternals"&nbsp;
replaced the typical Marvel theme with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.340
something reminiscent of a vintage&nbsp;
Western. "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.200
put a power ballad spin on it. But Marvel&nbsp;
Studios' first ever special presentation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.760
the Halloween special "Werewolf by Night,"&nbsp;
made the most significant changes to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:42.060
status quo with its new title graphic, its black&nbsp;
and white claw slashes, and its screams and howls.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.440
"The Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special"&nbsp;
continues this emerging tradition with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.060
its Christmas-themed opener. As The Pogues'&nbsp;
Christmas song "Fairytale of New York" plays,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:56.400
the usual comic graphics of Marvel superheroes&nbsp;
are interspersed with images of Christmas trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.680
garlands, kids ice skating, and, of&nbsp;
course, the big guy himself: Santa Claus.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.940
While the "Werewolf by Night" opener ends with&nbsp;
some black and white flashes of lightning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.480
the intro of "The Guardians of the&nbsp;
Galaxy Holiday Special" ends with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.100
the words "Marvel Studios" lit up in red&nbsp;
and green Christmas lights. These cheeky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.140
alterations aren't just a nod to the season.&nbsp;
Santa is actually part of Marvel Comics' canon.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.660
On the subject of music choices, "The Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy Holiday Special" features two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:30.480
live performances by professional musicians.&nbsp;
First up, alternative country band Old '97s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.160
are decked out in holiday attire. They've been&nbsp;
transformed into four different alien species,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.880
all of whom are playing their Earth&nbsp;
instruments for the first time. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.381
do this as they try to write a new song and&nbsp;
"historical document" about human Christmas.

00:01:43.381 --> 00:01:48.000
"Everything I know about Christmas, I&nbsp;
learned from Rocket, who learned from Cosmo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.286
who learned from Kraglin, who learned from you."

00:01:50.286 --> 00:01:53.580
That new song, "I Don't Know What&nbsp;
Christmas Is (But Christmastime Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:58.620
Here)," is full of hilarious misinterpretations&nbsp;
of Christmas stories and symbols. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:04.500
the alien band thinks that if children misbehave,&nbsp;
Santa puts dung in their socks, as opposed to coal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.000
in their stockings, which a frustrated Peter&nbsp;
Quill insists isn't "part of the lore" at all.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.020
Later, Kevin Bacon joins the Old&nbsp;
'97s to perform one of the group's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.020
pre-existing holiday numbers,&nbsp;
"Here It Is Christmas Time."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.240
Bacon isn't just a movie star and the subject&nbsp;
of the game Six Degrees of Kevin Bacon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:26.400
he's also a member of the band The Bacon Brothers&nbsp;
alongside his sibling Michael. The Bacon Brothers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:32.220
play a similar style of country folk rock music&nbsp;
to the Old '97s, so when this fictionalized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:36.480
version of the actor chooses to stay of his own&nbsp;
volition to celebrate the holidays on Knowhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.220
he picks up a guitar and fits right in with&nbsp;
the alien entertainment. The holiday special's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.680
soundtrack includes some other fun auditory Easter&nbsp;
eggs, too, like The Strokes' Julian Casablancas'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.902
rendition of the "Saturday Night Live"&nbsp;
Christmas song "I Wish It Was Christmas Today."

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.980
Writer and director James Gunn said that "The&nbsp;
Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special" will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.240
fill in some important narrative gaps&nbsp;
and prepare fans for "Vol. 3," which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:05.100
is scheduled to premiere in May of 2023.&nbsp;
Those appear to be these two new facts:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:10.080
The Guardians are the proud new owners of&nbsp;
Knowhere, and Mantis is Peter Quill's half-sister.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.820
Let's start with Knowhere. Viewers might not&nbsp;
realize that this is where they are when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.960
special begins, but Nebula tosses off a line&nbsp;
in which she explains that they've purchased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.580
the world that was once a Celestial's skull&nbsp;
from the Collector. We also see Knowhere in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.500
the background as Mantis and Drax fly away.&nbsp;
This confirms that Taneleer Tivan is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.180
alive and strongly implies that Knowhere will&nbsp;
be at least the partial setting of "Vol. 3."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.620
By the looks of it, the Guardians have done a&nbsp;
commendable job of rehabilitating the one-time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.060
mining colony and outpost into a tight-knit&nbsp;
community that's beginning to thrive again.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:46.440
As for Mantis, she's afraid to tell Peter&nbsp;
the truth about their relationship because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:51.480
she suspects it might remind him of his awful&nbsp;
father, Ego, and his mother's death at Ego's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.900
hand. Of course, Peter is thrilled&nbsp;
to have someone he can call family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.169
but it remains to be seen how their kinship&nbsp;
will impact the Guardians going forward.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.600
News broke that Maria Bakalova had&nbsp;
been cast in "Guardians of the Galaxy:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.100
Vol. 3" shortly after her star-making&nbsp;
performance in the second "Borat" movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:13.320
though nobody knew in what capacity. While she's&nbsp;
expected to play a much larger role in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:18.060
she has a fun cameo-sized role in two scenes&nbsp;
of the holiday special as the new voice of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:22.800
Cosmo the Spacedog. Cosmo has appeared&nbsp;
in the MCU before in "Guardians of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.240
Galaxy" where the dog is behind glass as&nbsp;
part of the Collector's collection. Cosmo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.340
also appears in the end credits of "Vol. 2"&nbsp;
and "What If... T'Challa Became a Star-Lord?"

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:36.600
The character originated in the comics,&nbsp;
where he's male and part of the Russian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:41.340
space program. The dog was based on a real&nbsp;
canine space explorer, who also happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:47.340
to be female. With Bulgarian comedian and actor&nbsp;
Bakalova's casting, Cosmo has been gender-swapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:53.700
retroactively rendering her female in her previous&nbsp;
MCU appearances. But, presumably, she retains the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:58.560
same backstory. The already species-diverse&nbsp;
"Guardians of the Galaxy" can only get more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:04.063
delightfully absurd with the addition of the&nbsp;
uproariously funny Bakalova as Cosmo the Spacedog.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:09.540
Sending Mantis and Drax to Hollywood created a&nbsp;
perfect opportunity for James Gunn and company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:14.280
to have fun at their own industry's expense.&nbsp;
The two most socially inept Guardians walk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.300
confidently down Hollywood Boulevard in&nbsp;
their search for the hero Kevin Bacon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.100
but they pause in front of the famous&nbsp;
TCL Chinese Theatre. In a fun Easter egg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:27.240
the actors who play the two Guardians have put&nbsp;
their real handprints and signatures in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.620
concrete just to the right of where Mantis and&nbsp;
Drax are standing during their photo session.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:36.300
Instead of Chris Evans or Scarlett Johansson&nbsp;
in their Captain America or Black Widow suits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:41.340
we see people in Spirit Halloween-quality Avengers&nbsp;
costumes posing for pictures with tourists.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.500
Besides Cap and Natasha, there's an&nbsp;
Ant-Man, a Captain Marvel, a Thor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.060
and a Jack Sparrow for good measure. Mantis&nbsp;
and Drax mistake the counterfeit Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:55.500
America for the real Steve Rogers, which&nbsp;
leads to an embarrassing moment. But soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.900
they realize these selfie-happy MCU fans are&nbsp;
a money-making opportunity, and they gladly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.422
snap some group pics before continuing their&nbsp;
quest for the best Christmas present ever.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:09.180
If you look closely at one banner in&nbsp;
particular near Hollywood Boulevard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:13.920
it advertises Kingo's latest project. In&nbsp;
our world, we might all be watching "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:18.300
Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special,"&nbsp;
but in the world of the MCU, the public is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:23.220
getting "Kingo's Christmas." A large vertical&nbsp;
billboard marketing the actor-slash-Eternal's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:27.420
special can be seen on the side of a building&nbsp;
before Mantis and Drax enter the bar.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.920
Kingo, played by Kumail Nanjiani,&nbsp;
is an immortal being, but in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:35.820
"Eternals," he's biding his time on Earth&nbsp;
as a celebrity who keeps reinventing himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:39.840
as his own son or grandson, so as&nbsp;
not to arouse suspicion about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:45.600
eternal youth. The MCU's version of Kingo really&nbsp;
enjoys being a celebrity. He also fits Mantis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.820
Drax, and Nebula's impression of actors as&nbsp;
self-absorbed fame chasers who aren't heroes.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.600
"He's an actor! He's never actually saved anyone!"

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.100
"But actors are repugnant!"

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.337
"I know!"

00:06:57.337 --> 00:07:02.374
This is because Kingo doesn't show up to help the&nbsp;
rest of the Eternals in the climax of that film.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.680
Another Easter egg that works as a multilayered&nbsp;
joke with multiple meanings is the inclusion of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:12.840
celebrity star maps. When a drunk Mantis and Drax&nbsp;
come to a dead end in their hunt for Kevin Bacon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:17.940
the owner of a souvenir shop overhears their&nbsp;
conversation and offers the alien duo a map of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:22.920
stars. These maps are big business in Hollywood,&nbsp;
though they're not always reliable, so the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:27.780
idea that Mantis and Drax could use one to find&nbsp;
Kevin Bacon's house is a joke in and of itself.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.580
Since she lost her money, Mantis deploys her&nbsp;
powers to steal the map and the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:36.780
cash in the woman's fanny pack. A graphic&nbsp;
appears onscreen that purports to show the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:40.740
locations of the residences of a handful&nbsp;
of celebrities. There's Queen Latifah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:45.540
John Cena, Arnold Schwarzenegger, and&nbsp;
a photo of a young Mark-Paul Gosselaar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.380
from his "Saved by the Bell" days. Once&nbsp;
Mantis and Drax get to Kevin Bacon's house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:54.360
the house number, 1988, is a reference to&nbsp;
the year Peter Quill was taken into space&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:59.760
by Yondu. Star Maps is also a sort of double&nbsp;
entendre since the Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:05.160
exist in space and frequently travel between&nbsp;
planets using maps of various star systems.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.300
"The Guardians of the Galaxy"&nbsp;
movies largely take place in space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:14.160
and many scenes take place aboard spaceships.&nbsp;
That means there are tons of vehicles in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.540
"Guardians" movies, and most of them have&nbsp;
pretty innovative and recognizable designs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:24.660
as well as clever names. Peter Quill started&nbsp;
with the Milano, named after '80s and '90's TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:29.700
star Alyssa Milano. He upgraded to the&nbsp;
Benatar, named for singer Pat Benatar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.560
which can be seen in "Avengers: Infinity War,"&nbsp;
"Avengers: Endgame," and "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.820
"The Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special"&nbsp;
introduces the Guardians' newest ship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:44.580
the Bowie, named after rock icon David Bowie.&nbsp;
Star-Lord commands his crew to get Kevin Bacon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:48.600
aboard the Bowie and fly him safely back&nbsp;
to Earth so that they're not on the hook&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:52.980
for human trafficking anymore. But once in the&nbsp;
driver and passenger seats of the spacecraft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:57.600
Kraglin and Kevin Bacon have a heart-to-heart.&nbsp;
Kevin decides to stay a little longer to teach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:02.220
everyone on Knowhere the meaning of Christmas.&nbsp;
The Bowie first appeared in the comics in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:07.380
so the holiday special is simply making the&nbsp;
ship officially part of the MCU's canon.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:12.000
Once everyone starts exchanging gifts, the&nbsp;
Easter eggs in "The Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.560
Holiday Special" get even wittier&nbsp;
and more self-referential. Nebula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.780
who isn't exactly known for being warm and fuzzy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:23.820
gives Rocket a sizable rectangular box.&nbsp;
He opens it to discover a metal appendage.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:27.720
"Bucky's arm?" he asks, to which&nbsp;
Nebula says, "Merry Christmas."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.980
She doesn't want to acknowledge it, but&nbsp;
this is an incredibly thoughtful gift,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:37.140
not to mention an expensive one – Bucky's&nbsp;
most recent arm was made out of Vibranium.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:41.640
In "Avengers: Infinity War," Bucky and&nbsp;
Rocket fight side by side. At one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:46.020
the former lifts the latter into the air and they&nbsp;
take out their surrounding enemies with a circular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:51.780
barrage of gunfire. Afterward, Rocket tries to&nbsp;
negotiate a price for Bucky's gun…and his arm.

00:09:52.075 --> 00:09:53.135
"How much for the gun?"

00:09:53.135 --> 00:09:54.120
"It's not for sale."

00:09:54.625 --> 00:09:56.725
"Okay, how much for the arm?"

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:02.160
This callback to "Infinity War" also calls&nbsp;
back to the first "Guardians" movie. In it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.120
Rocket instructs the newly banded Guardians&nbsp;
to steal a prosthetic leg in their attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:09.480
to break out of prison. When it comes&nbsp;
time to put their plan into action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:13.360
he reveals that he didn't need the&nbsp;
leg, he just thought it would be funny.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:17.880
An older teenage Groot carves little&nbsp;
wooden dioramas for all of his friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:22.200
in the "Guardians" holiday special. He hands&nbsp;
out the wrapped boxes and each member of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:26.340
Guardians opens theirs. Mantis' diorama&nbsp;
depicts the beginning of the live-action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:30.900
part of the special when the Guardians were&nbsp;
standing on a balcony talking about how Yondu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:35.700
ruined Christmas. Peter Quill gets a carving&nbsp;
of Mantis and Drax chasing a terrified Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:40.920
Bacon down the street. Drax receives a miniature&nbsp;
version of himself flipping over a police car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:46.200
Nebula's scene recreates the moment everyone&nbsp;
gave Kevin Bacon, still under Mantis' control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:50.940
to Peter Quill as a gift. In other words, the&nbsp;
presents Groot has given his friends tell the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:55.920
story of the holiday special. That leaves&nbsp;
Kraglin, who opens his box last. For him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:01.440
Groot has carved a small Kraglin opening an even&nbsp;
smaller Kraglin opening an even smaller Kraglin.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:07.080
The "Guardians of the Galaxy" films have given the&nbsp;
MCU some of its weirdest supporting and featured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:12.600
characters, and the wackiest might be Taserface.&nbsp;
This numbskulled and aggressive space pirate has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:17.460
been in the comics since 1990, but he made&nbsp;
his MCU debut in "Guardians of the Galaxy:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:23.220
Vol. 2" when he tried to stage a mutiny and&nbsp;
came into conflict with Rocket Raccoon. Rocket&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:28.431
repeatedly mocks his name, to which Taserface&nbsp;
infamously replies with a full-bodied shout.

00:11:28.642 --> 00:11:30.742
"It's metaphorical!"

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:38.040
Taserface didn't make it out of that film alive,&nbsp;
but he popped up in "What If...?" where, in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:43.080
alternate reality, he and Kraglin pick up T'Challa&nbsp;
instead of Peter Quill. We don't see an animated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:47.700
Taserface in "The Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday&nbsp;
Special," but the character still gets a shoutout.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:51.360
As Yondu goes through the garbage&nbsp;
can of presents and decorations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:54.780
that he destroyed and threw away&nbsp;
in a fit of anti-Christmas rage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.780 --> 00:12:00.480
we can see that one package has been designated&nbsp;
for Taserface. The sloppy handwriting is likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:05.377
a clue that young Peter remembered Taserface&nbsp;
and got the angry Ravager something special.

